  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the following radioactive decays</p><p>I. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mprescripts/><mn>92</mn><none/></mmultiscripts><msub><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></mrow></mover><mn>90</mn></msub><mi>Th</mi></math>&nbsp;and</p><p>II. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>90</mn></msub><mi>Th</mi><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></mrow></mover><mmultiscripts><mi>Ra</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>88</mn><none></none></mmultiscripts></math></p><p>In which case group of parent and daughter elements remains unchanged.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
