  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For the following radioactive decays</p><p>I. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>92</mn><none></none></mmultiscripts><msub><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></mrow></mover><mn>90</mn></msub><mi>Th</mi></math> and<br />II. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>Th</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>90</mn><none></none></mmultiscripts><msub><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></mrow></mover><mn>88</mn></msub><mi>Ra</mi></math></p><p>&nbsp;In&nbsp;both Uranium and Thorium belongs to IIIB group.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo></math> Elements with atomic number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>103</mn></math> belongs to same group, i.e. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>III</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>rd</mi></math> group (i.e. actinoids).</p>",
    "image": null
  },
